# EnTT components live in components.hpp

Any struct stored in the registry (`emplace<T>`, `view<T>`, `get<T>`, `try_get<T>`, `all_of<T>`, ...) is defined in a `components.hpp`. Never in a `.cpp`, a `config.hpp`, a `visual.hpp`, or any other header.

Pick the narrowest level that covers every user of the component:

- `core/components.hpp` — used by more than one kind of module (`Position`, `Age`, `Energy`, `Visual`).
- `plant/components.hpp` — shared by the plant modules (`plant::PlantTypeIndex`).
- `agent/components.hpp` — shared by agent modules (`agent::Agent`, `agent::EpisodeCycles`, `agent::Inactive`).
- `<module>/components.hpp` — owned by one module (`random_plant::Fertility`, `energy_storage_plant::Lineage`, `ql_agent::QlAgent`, `c51_agent::C51Agent`).

## Rules

- Before adding a component, look in all three levels for one with the same fields. If two modules need the same data, define it once at the shared level and use it from both.
- Marker tags stay one per module (`random_plant::Plant`, `energy_storage_plant::EnergyPlant`, `ql_agent::QlAgent`, `c51_agent::C51Agent`). A view over a shared component must include the module's marker, otherwise it also matches other modules' entities. Occupancy/vision over any agent uses the shared `agent::Agent` marker.
- Enums and aliases a component needs may sit next to it (`plant::PlantKind`, `random_plant::ResidueKind`).
- Code that creates or destroys a component's entities belongs to the module that owns the component, and other modules call it. Example: `random_plant/residue.hpp` owns `PlantResidue` entities; the grid calls `random_plant::leave_residue`.

## Example

```cpp
// BAD: the same component defined once per module
namespace random_plant { struct PlantType { PlantKind kind; }; }
namespace energy_storage_plant { struct PlantTypeIndex { PlantKind kind; }; }

// GOOD: defined once in plant/components.hpp, filtered by the module marker
auto view = registry.view<const random_plant::Plant, const plant::PlantTypeIndex>();
```

## When planning

List every component the change adds or moves and the `components.hpp` it goes in.
